# The repo-root .gitignore ignores `.env.*` wholesale, which would swallow the
# checked-in template below. A .gitignore deeper in the tree wins, so this
# single negation is what keeps `build/.env.example` under version control.
#
# `build/.env` itself stays ignored (root rule `.env`) — it holds real
# credentials. Copy, do not commit:  cp build/.env.example build/.env
!.env.example
